import json,statistics as st,html,sys,math
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(sys.argv[1]);rows=[json.loads(s) for s in (p/'games.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()];assert len(rows)==60
mean=lambda v:round(st.mean(v),2) if v else None
summ=[]
for players in [None,2,3,4]:
 for cohort in [None,'self','mixed']:
  a=[r for r in rows if (players is None or r['players']==players) and (cohort is None or r['cohort']==cohort)];f=[r for r in a if r.get('endReason')=='finish'];valid=[r for r in a if r['status']!='failed'];prices=sorted(x for r in valid for x in r['prices'])
  summ.append(dict(players=players or 'all',cohort=cohort or 'all',n=len(a),finished=len(f),stalled=sum(r['status']=='stalled' for r in a),failed=sum(r['status']=='failed' for r in a),censored=sum(r['status']=='censored' for r in a),gap=mean([r['range'] for r in f]),third=mean([r['thirdLag'] for r in f]),actions=mean([r['actions'] for r in valid]),zero=mean([r['zero'] for r in f]),auctionMean=mean(prices),auctionMedian=st.median(prices) if prices else None,auctionP90=prices[min(len(prices)-1,int(.9*len(prices)))] if prices else None,noSales=sum(r['noSales'] for r in valid)))
metrics={'summary':summ,'actionMeans':{t:mean([r['types'][t] for r in rows if r['status']!='failed']) for t in ['call','valueAction','changeFounder','raiseMoney']}}
(p/'metrics.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics,indent=2));print(json.dumps(metrics,indent=2))
if not (p/'sample-review.json').exists():sys.exit()
reviews=json.loads((p/'sample-review.json').read_text());attempts=json.loads((p/'sample-index.json').read_text());manifest=json.loads((p/'manifest.json').read_text());allrow=summ[0];completed=[a for a in attempts if a['status']=='complete']
def table(rows,keys):return '<table><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+html.escape(k)+'</th>' for k in keys)+'</tr>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(r[k]) if r.get(k) is not None else '—')+'</td>' for k in keys)+'</tr>' for r in rows)+'</table>'
body=f'<h1>v136: the hand now dwindles, but draws can lock the game</h1><p>Nine cards/company · bland/mild/spicy · improved auction/endgame bots · draws only at leg end</p><p><b>{allrow["finished"]}/60 games reached 24; {allrow["stalled"]}/60 stalled.</b> A stall means every player ran out of deal-flow cards before the next leg boundary, with cards still in the deck. No automatic refill or settlement was added. These cases are not counted as tighter finishes.</p>'
body+='<h2>What changed</h2><p>Public cards refill as before. Five private deal-flow cards initially; retain leftovers and draw three only when a leg ends. All four public values and all four founders are visible; the full private hand is grouped by company beside the drawer. Dice selectors show only bland, mild and spicy; numerical zero is separate from a fumble.</p><p>Bots estimate the auction winner and payment, evaluate the resulting portfolio and terminal score margin, and cap bids using post-payment outcomes. The previously documented losing terminal offer is covered by a regression. Conflict no longer receives an unconditional positive bonus. Cached forecasts match the original price-specific resolver; no hidden hands or sealed bids enter the estimates. Long-term planning, opponent bid prediction and value effects remain heuristic.</p>'
body+='<h2>Results</h2>'+table([r for r in summ if r['cohort']=='all'],['players','n','finished','stalled','gap','third','actions','zero'])
body+='<p>Gap=first–last; third=first–third, in spaces. Both, and zero-payout counts, include only games reaching 24. Action means include completed and stalled games, not bid/acknowledgement steps. Sparse finishes cannot establish spread improvement. Target: ≥95% reach24, mean first–last≤16 and first–third≤8. Completion fails decisively.</p>'
body+='<p><b>Why the deck size does not solve this:</b> only five cards per player are accessible before the first leg. The remaining deck cannot help until three companies reach8. Auctions that fail to sell, value actions, capital calls and hires all consume those limited actions; concentrated movement can advance one or two companies without unlocking the next draw. The rule has a circular dependency: more movement needs cards, but more cards require movement.</p><p>This run changes bots, dice and draw timing together. It is not a causal bot-only comparison with v135. The interrupted run-01 was retained for audit and excluded after forecast-performance optimization.</p>'
body+='<details><summary>Action usage, auctions and policy breakdown</summary>'+table([metrics['actionMeans']],list(metrics['actionMeans']))+table([r for r in summ if r['players']=='all'],['cohort','n','finished','stalled','auctionMean','auctionMedian','auctionP90','noSales'])+table([r for r in summ if r['cohort']!='all' and r['players']!='all'],['players','cohort','n','finished','stalled','gap','third','actions'])+'</details>'
body+=f'<h2>Sample review status</h2><p>{len(completed)} of ten planned sample slots produced a completed game within the frozen eight-attempt-per-slot budget. All {len(attempts)} attempts, including stalls, are retained and replay-verified. '+('The ten-completed-game validation target was not met; this is a failure diagnostic, not a completed balance validation. ' if len(completed)<10 else '')+'Reviews below cover the fixed initial attempts and any completed retry selected for review. No stalled game is assigned a winner.</p>'
for r in reviews:
 seed=r['seed'];g=json.loads((p/f'samples/{seed}.json').read_text());m=g['meta']
 body+=f'<details><summary>Game {seed} · {m["players"]} players · {m["cohort"]} · {m["status"]}</summary><p>{html.escape(r["review"])}</p><p><a href="samples/{seed}.json">Full events and recorded decisions</a> · <a href="samples/{seed}-replay.json">Importable replay</a></p><details><summary>Complete ordered event trace</summary><pre>'+html.escape('\n'.join(f'E{i} '+json.dumps(e,ensure_ascii=False) for i,e in enumerate(g['events'])))+'</pre></details></details>'
body+='<details><summary>Reproduce and audit</summary><p>60 primary games: seeds8101–8110, 2/3/4 players, balanced self-play and mixed policies with rotating lineups. Completed and stalled traces replay to identical logs and scores. A stall is a legal dead-end under the requested rules, distinguished from an exception or decision cutoff.</p><p>Source hash: <code>'+manifest['source']+'</code></p><p><a href="manifest.json">Frozen protocol</a> · <a href="games.jsonl">Raw primary games</a> · <a href="metrics.json">Metrics</a> · <a href="sample-index.json">All sample attempts</a> · <a href="runtime.json">Runtime</a> · <a href="source/scripts/mild-dice-study.js">Runner and source snapshot</a></p><pre>node scripts/mild-dice-study.js NEW_DIRECTORY\npython3 scripts/mild-dice-report.py NEW_DIRECTORY</pre><p>Rendering reviews requires the authored sample-review.json. No rules were changed during run-02.</p></details>'
(p/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>v136 nine-card study</title><style>body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;background:#f8f6ef;color:#1c2925;max-width:1050px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:30px}table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;display:block;overflow:auto;margin:16px 0}th,td{padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc;text-align:left}th{background:#e2e8da}details{padding:16px;margin:18px 0;background:white;border:1px solid #ccd3c7;border-radius:8px}summary{font-weight:650;cursor:pointer}pre,code{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}a{color:#155e47}</style>'+body+'</html>')
